{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"336447de80c65b67952d245a4c2480dbea373c796f384b521148a0541870cd9f","slug":"host-disks","location":"/guide/host-disks.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Real hard disks","content_includes_title":false,"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Andrew Hutchings","given":"Andrew","family":"Hutchings"},"name":"Andrew Hutchings","id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"}],"github":"https://github.com/CopperlineHQ/Copperline","keywords":["amiga","emulator","ocs","ecs","rust"],"numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"source_url":"https://github.com/CopperlineHQ/Copperline/blob/main/docs/guide/host-disks.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/CopperlineHQ/Copperline/edit/main/docs/guide/host-disks.md","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"host-disks.md","url":"/docs/build/host-disks-80f2ded31be79e264b69f4b260c3e41d.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":8,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Copperline can give the emulated machine a real disk of this computer’s\ninstead of a hard-drive image -- any disk it can see: a card in a reader, a\nUSB drive, a drive on a SATA port. The Amiga sees the medium as it is, with\nits own Rigid Disk Block, its own partitions, its own filesystem. Nothing is\ncopied or converted, so a card taken out of an A1200 boots the same Workbench\nit booted five minutes earlier.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"eGVHAa37Sa"}],"key":"jnOm5NkwAh"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This writes to whole physical media rather than to a file, where a mistake\ncosts somebody their only copy of an Amiga’s system disk. The rules below are\nnot configurable.","position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"key":"sTRWVuJeYm"}],"key":"KbI8zdCDst"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"What you can attach","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"hh1CoBUOix"}],"identifier":"what-you-can-attach","label":"What you can attach","html_id":"what-you-can-attach","implicit":true,"key":"VnLDO6Kk2g"},{"type":"code","lang":"sh","value":"copperline --list-disks","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"key":"smwJrAxfwY"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"names every disk, how big it is, and anything you need to know before\nchoosing one:","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"UfQHyT7Ug9"}],"key":"f6wRXu4OwA"},{"type":"code","lang":"text","value":"Host disks (name one to --host-disk, or as [[host_disk]] device):\n  sdb        Generic MassStorageClass (31.9 GB)\n  sdc        ATA Samsung SSD 870 (500.1 GB) [internal]\n  sda        ATA Ubuntu Linux-0 S (68.7 GB) [system disk, internal, mounted: /]  -- cannot be used","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"Z3DbSifxBa"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Listing reads nothing from any medium and needs no privileges, so it is safe\nto run at any time.","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"key":"EKFLRBFHwr"}],"key":"FPmvyhkhF5"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every disk is offered except ","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"wCSCtiB1ES"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"the one this computer is running from","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"e3tQzLX2OW"}],"key":"kowCQXrajs"},{"type":"text","value":", which\nis refused by name however it is asked for -- launcher, config file, or\ncommand line. It is still listed, marked ","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"IHlsHVVDVS"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cannot be used","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"I8gB9WKhT6"},{"type":"text","value":", because a disk\nthat silently vanished would just look like a bug. Which disk that is gets\nworked out afresh on every run from your machine’s own layout, following the\nrunning system through whatever sits under it: LVM and LUKS on Linux, an APFS\ncontainer down to the drive it is stored on for macOS. If a layout cannot be\ntraced, nothing is offered at all.","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"sRwtGVk7Jl"}],"key":"ouQIeGnNeK"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disks on an internal bus are labelled ","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"a6dFraC9qD"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"internal","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"b8sVpUzlrH"},{"type":"text","value":" and sorted last, but they\nare yours to use. And no RDB is ever invented over a disk that has none: an\nAmiga disk carries its own partition table, and one that does not is a disk\nCopperline will not pretend to understand.","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"XTr5lUOvn6"}],"key":"r7LvxWasKg"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attaching one","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"col