in a configuration file:","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"key":"peYzy6mgET"}],"key":"EGgaLxs9eS"},{"type":"code","lang":"toml","value":"[[host_disk]]\ndevice = \"sdb\"                 # last name shown by --list-disks\nfingerprint = \"v1-...\"         # opaque identity written by the launcher\nattach = \"ide-master\"          # ide-master (default), ide-slave, or scsi0..scsi6\nread_only = true               # the default; false explicitly allows writes","position":{"start":{"line":62,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"key":"Ky8LmpkuLQ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"device","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"key":"nDXHdTaRJj"},{"type":"text","value":" is the host’s current enumeration name, exactly as ","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"key":"TifJ3OOKLf"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--list-disks","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"key":"cPuof3dLlS"},{"type":"text","value":"\nprints it: ","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"key":"jvYYySU8fG"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sdb","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"key":"NGHOex8GlI"},{"type":"text","value":" on Linux, ","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"key":"mAAbK2eqx8"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"disk4","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"key":"QgwRIL3YdN"},{"type":"text","value":" on macOS, or ","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"key":"MN7LQ12UdD"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PhysicalDrive1","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"key":"BG1DYDwD4X"},{"type":"text","value":" on Windows.\nThose names can change when disks are attached in a different order. The\nlauncher therefore saves ","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"key":"m1F3z1nv73"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fingerprint","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"key":"qtZtu0O64n"},{"type":"text","value":", an opaque identity made from the\ndisk’s reported serial/model and geometry. On the next run the fingerprint is\nauthoritative: Copperline follows the same disk to a changed name only when\nexactly one attached disk matches it, and refuses a missing or ambiguous\nmatch rather than guessing. Keep the value the launcher wrote; do not invent\nor copy one between disks.","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"key":"Hj3f7TWBCs"}],"key":"YOkheE9JIN"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":80,"column":1},"end":{"line":85,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Older and hand-written entries may omit ","position":{"start":{"line":80,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"key":"E1ybmxMgCj"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fingerprint","position":{"start":{"line":80,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"key":"v1yi2tEnfN"},{"type":"text","value":"; they use an exact\n","position":{"start":{"line":80,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"key":"T149F1Al2m"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"device","position":{"start":{"line":80,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"key":"MtlmJeRdw5"},{"type":"text","value":" lookup and cannot follow a renamed disk. To add one, select and mount\nthe disk afresh in the launcher, then save or launch; merely opening and\nsaving the old entry deliberately preserves the missing fingerprint. A disk\nthat cannot be resolved leaves that drive slot empty and the machine starts\nanyway, as a real Amiga does with an absent drive.","position":{"start":{"line":80,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"key":"Pc4vYRBXUT"}],"key":"p8w716UhOT"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":87,"column":1},"end":{"line":94,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persisted permission to write is deliberately narrower than fingerprint\nmatching. Removable media is always treated as weak, even if its USB bridge\nreports a serial: that value often identifies the reader rather than the card\ninside it. The same is true of any fixed disk without a credible serial or\nWWN. A fingerprint can still resolve either kind for read-only use, but select\nand mount the physical disk afresh in the launcher before every writable\nsession. Only a fixed, non-removable disk with a credible serial/WWN may reopen\nwritable from persisted configuration.","position":{"start":{"line":87,"column":1},"end":{"line":87,"column":1}},"key":"grlmKRWHPM"}],"key":"i594tuh4mK"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":96,"column":1},"end":{"line":100,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Omitting ","position":{"start":{"line":96,"column":1},"end":{"line":96,"column":1}},"key":"DykAybHOqd"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"read_only","position":{"start":{"line":96,"column":1},"end":{"line":96,"column":1}},"key":"bRYfc4gLz0"},{"type":"text","value":" is safe: it now means read-only. This intentionally makes\nolder configs that omitted the key read-only too; set ","position":{"start":{"line":96,"column":1},"end":{"line":96,"column":1}},"key":"fcVW5P9vZl"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"read_only = false","position":{"start":{"line":96,"column":1},"end":{"line":96,"column":1}},"key":"irC5EcVdTI"},{"type":"text","value":"\nonly after checking the selected disk. The command-line flags describe a\nchoice made for this run, so ","position":{"start":{"line":96,"column":1},"end":{"line":96,"column":1}},"key":"FxnXzGWJ42"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--host-disk","position":{"start":{"line":96,"column":1},"end":{"line":96,"column":1}},"key":"Z0ep9sP5Zs"},{"type":"text","value":" is explicitly read-write and\n","position":{"start":{"line":96,"column":1},"end":{"line":96,"column":1}},"key":"DHzg8AGXVy"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--host-disk-read-only","position":{"start":{"line":96,"column":1},"end":{"line":96,"column":1}},"key":"ygKjVu4g3t"},{"type":"text","value":" is protected.","position":{"start":{"line":96,"column":1},"end":{"line":96,"column":1}},"key":"mVENNcvVRp"}],"key":"ZCwqfzDo2Z"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":102,"column":1},"end":{"line":102,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read-only first","position":{"start":{"line":102,"column":1},"end":{"line":102,"column":1}},"key":"iWnDwqb6mt"}],"identifier":"read-only-first","label":"Read-only first","html_id":"read-only-first","implicit":true,"key":"GrYIh9m8ug"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":105,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attach a disk read-only the first time. It costs one boot and tells you more\nthan anything else:","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"key":"WLbydl8eoU"}],"key":"qb8EdWeMzf"},{"type":"code","lang":"sh","value":"copperline --model A1200 --fast 8M KICK31.ROM --host-disk-read-only sdb","position":{"start":{"line":107,"column":1},"end":{"line":109,"column":1}},"key":"GgQyc5mLEJ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":111,"column":1},"end":{"line":113,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"An Amiga filesystem writes when it mounts -- PFS marks the volume in use --\nso a ","position":{"start":{"line":111,"column":1},"end":{"line":111,"column":1}},"key":"QfIHcBUXY7"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":111,"column":1},"end":{"line":111,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"correct","position":{"start":{"line":111,"column":1},"end":{"line":111,"column":1}},"key":"rZBWh0iwA8"}],"key":"VRfsK2o2M0"},{"type":"text","value":" read-only attach boots far enough to raise the guest’s own\nwrite error, and the log names the same block:","position":{"start":{"line":111,"column":1},"end":{"line":111,"column":1}},"key":"i1JGcN5BGf"}],"key":"AmgDg9mV1c"},{"type":"code","lang":"text","value":"blockdev: sdb is attached read-only, so the guest's write to sector 1026146\n          was refused; tick R/W (or set `read_only = false`) to let it write","position":{"start":{"line":115,"column":1},"end":{"line":118,"column":1}},"key":"lJJyTgGvZK"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":120,"column":1},"end":{"line":121,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"That proves the read path end to end. Attach it read-write and it should\nreach Workbench with no requester at all.","position":{"start":{"line":120,"column":1},"end":{"line":120,"column":1}},"key":"VvrOwCtYUY"}],"key":"tMRDwIzkHt"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":123,"column":1},"end":{"line":123,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"While the machine has it","position":{"start":{"line":123,"column":1},"end":{"line":123,"column":1}},"key":"BYBcirkoaE"}],"identifier":"while-the-machine-has-it","label":"While the machine has it","html_id":"while-the-machine-has-it","implicit":true,"key":"TcuolN8I0t"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":125,"column":1},"end":{"line":130,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The disk is taken from the host completely. Volumes mounted from it are\nunmounted first -- the host writing its own metadata under a guest that\ncannot account for it changing is a hazard either way -- and the medium stays\nthe machine’s until you give it back. If something else still has a file open\non the disk, the attach fails and says so rather than taking it out from\nunderneath.","position":{"start":{"line":125,"column":1},"end":{"line":125,"column":1}},"key":"tsEnUTCKWV"}],"key":"ecmOJaNv0Q"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":132,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"It is taken once, at ","position":{"start":{"line":132,"column":1},"end":{"line":132,"column":1}},"key":"P9QqaK1KSV"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":132,"column":1},"end":{"line":132,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mount","position":{"start":{"line":132,"column":1},"end":{"line":132,"column":1}},"key":"qGX6B6ZCTv"}],"key":"VsJSEYLhaS"},{"type":"text","value":" (or when a configuration-driven run first\nstarts), and stays taken for the rest of the session. Powering the emulated\nmachine off and on again does not ask for permission a second time.\n","position":{"start":{"line":132,"column":1},"end":{"line":132,"column":1}},"key":"G8JwrxZI1p"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":132,"column":1},"end":{"line":132,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unmount","position":{"start":{"line":132,"column":1},"end":{"line":132,"column":1}},"key":"UkACv22cIY"}],"key":"xF8qR5BgFF"},{"type":"text","value":" -- on the Host Disk page, or beside the drive on the Storage page\n-- hands the disk back, and so does quitting.","position":{"start":{"line":132,"column":1},"end":{"line":132,"column":1}},"key":"i4y0994V7Z"}],"key":"aWF8C98M64"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":138,"column":1},"end":{"line":143,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Save states carry the same fingerprint. Loading one re-enumerates the host and\nreattaches only one unambiguous match; a changed ","position":{"start":{"line":138,"column":1},"end":{"line":138,"column":1}},"key":"Pro6wYpepf"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sdb","position":{"start":{"line":138,"column":1},"end":{"line":138,"column":1}},"key":"WVrYfA18RZ"},{"type":"text","value":"/","position":{"start":{"line":138,"column":1},"end":{"line":138,"column":1}},"key":"vvGswcSu5s"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"disk4","position":{"start":{"line":138,"column":1},"end":{"line":138,"column":1}},"key":"ak01QhIq7S"},{"type":"text","value":"/\n","position":{"start":{"line":138,"column":1},"end":{"line":138,"column":1}},"key":"oOYyFfWA29"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Physic